{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607051730-murakumo-cloud-fleet-hwmetrics-dashboard"
  :title "murakumo.cloud — live CPU/GPU/mem/disk fleet dashboard"
  :status "closed"
  :date "2026-07-05"
  :authoritative true
  :repos ["orgs/kotoba-lang/murakumo" "orgs/gftdcojp/local-murakumo"]
  :related ["90-docs/adr/2607051431-murakumo-cloud-live-inference-anthropic-bridge.md"]}

 :problem
 {:ask "visualize live CPU/GPU/storage utilization for the gad + murakumo fleet on murakumo.cloud in realtime"
  :found "no hardware-metrics collection existed at all — murakumo.infer/probe-node only reads mem/disk totals over SSH
          (sysctl hw.memsize, df, iogpu.wired_limit_mb), never utilization %; /itonami/perf is hardcoded benchmark
          data, not live; /infer/fleet is an anonymized append-only stream with no live producer"}

 :decisions
 {:1-precision-and-placement
  {:question "how precise, and where does the collector run?"
   :user-choice {:precision "full precision via powermetrics/root (not a no-root approximation)"
                 :placement "background daemon on gad (not an on-demand manual command)"
                 :access "public read (matches existing /itonami/perf, /infer/fleet transparency posture); write side token-gated"}
   :prereq-check "passwordless sudo for `powermetrics` already provisioned on every Apple M4 mesh node —
                  no new sudoers change needed. gad already holds SSH access to the whole mesh + the
                  cloudflared tunnel reaching api.murakumo.cloud, so it's the natural collector host."}

  :2-collector
  {:new-file "orgs/kotoba-lang/murakumo/tools/hwmetrics-report/hwmetrics-report.sh"
   :gad-local "CPU: 200ms /proc/stat delta (no root). GPU: /sys/class/drm/card1/device/{gpu_busy_percent,
              mem_info_vram_used,mem_info_vram_total} — amdgpu exposes these unprivileged. mem: free -b. disk: df -k /."
   :mac-workers "one ssh round-trip per node: `sudo -n powermetrics -n1 -i1000 --samplers cpu_power,gpu_power`
                (real E-Cluster/P-Cluster + GPU HW active residency) + vm_stat/sysctl/df. CPU% = core-count-
                weighted average of E/P cluster active residency."
   :concurrency-bug-caught-before-shipping
   {:found "serial SSH against fleet.edn's 10-node roster (4 of which are routinely offline/asleep) costs
           4×ConnectTimeout=16s alone — 21s measured wall-clock total, blowing past any sane report interval"
    :fix "all ~11 probes (gad + 10 workers) run concurrently as background jobs, collected via a tmpdir + wait;
         measured wall-clock dropped to ~2-4s"}
   :surprise-finding "worker CPU% reads ~90-100% on every node, consistently, across repeated samples — initially
                      suspected as a powermetrics short-sample measurement artifact (HW active residency ≠ Unix
                      CPU-idle%), but `top -l` confirmed the same ~90-100% independently: the same 10 Apple M4
                      minis (fleet.edn) also run `xmrig` as a standing Monero-mining fleet (see the `uriage`
                      skill) — genuinely real, continuous CPU load, not a bug. Exactly the kind of contention
                      this dashboard is meant to surface."
   :roster "WORKERS array is a static mirror of fleet.edn's :host list — fleet.edn stays the SSoT, both need
           updating together if the mesh roster changes."}

  :3-api-and-dashboard
  {:repo "orgs/gftdcojp/local-murakumo"
   :routes {:post "/infer/hwmetrics — Bearer MURAKUMO_METRICS_TOKEN gated (worker.cljs-only; the pure
                  routes.cljc layer has no header/env access, matching how /v1/messages auth also lives
                  only in worker.cljs). Overwrites a single `hwmetrics/latest` doc via IStore -put/-get —
                  NOT an append-only stream like /infer/fleet, since the collector posts every ~10s forever
                  and only the current reading is ever shown."
            :get "/infer/hwmetrics — public JSON, latest snapshot"
            :get-ui "/infer/hwmetrics/ui — public SSR page (local-murakumo.infer-view/fleet-page), inline
                    vanilla-JS poller (5s, no reagent/re-frame — this page has its own independent poll loop
                    over different state than /infer/ui's model-centric app; duplicating ~20 lines of render
                    logic in JS was simpler than threading a second state slice through the existing
                    single-page re-frame app)"}
   :tested "routes.cljc covered by a new JVM test (hwmetrics deftest: no-report-yet, POST overwrite semantics,
           /ui rendering incl. offline badge) — 26 tests / 202 assertions all green"}

  :4-secret-provisioning
  {:token "MURAKUMO_METRICS_TOKEN, openssl rand -hex 32"
   :stored ["1Password gftd.murakumo/METRICS_TOKEN (vault gftdcojp, API Credential category)"
            "Cloudflare Worker secret via `wrangler secret put`"
            "root-only /etc/murakumo-hwmetrics.env (mode 600) on gad, read by the systemd unit's EnvironmentFile"]}

  :5-systemd-on-gad
  {:script-path "/home/gad/murakumo/hwmetrics-report.sh"
   :unit "murakumo-hwmetrics.service (oneshot) + murakumo-hwmetrics.timer (OnBootSec 15s, OnUnitActiveSec 10s)"
   :verified "systemctl enable --now; journalctl confirmed clean 10s-interval runs (initial 404s before the
             Worker deploy landed, 201s after)"}}

 :consequences
 ["https://api.murakumo.cloud/infer/hwmetrics/ui shows live per-node CPU/GPU/mem/disk for gad + the Apple M4
   mesh, auto-refreshing every 5s, offline nodes clearly badged instead of silently missing"
  "surfaces a previously-invisible operational fact: the inference workers are concurrently mining Monero
   (xmrig), so their near-saturated CPU numbers are real contention, not idle headroom"
  "the collector script is the first hardware-utilization telemetry in either repo — prior /itonami/perf and
   /infer/fleet were static/anonymized; this is the pattern to extend if per-node GPU tok/s or per-request
   attribution is wanted later"]

 :follow-ups-not-done
 ["no historical retention/sparklines — only the single latest snapshot is stored (KV doc, not a stream);
   would need a bounded ring buffer if trend charts are wanted"
  "hwmetrics-report.sh's WORKERS array duplicates fleet.edn's :host list by hand — could be generated at
   `bb scripts/gen-west-manifest.bb`-adjacent tooling time instead of maintained by hand"
  "no alerting (e.g. a node flapping offline/online) — dashboard is read-only visualization, not monitoring"]

 :addendum-2026-07-05-part1-gpu-default
 {:change "swapped GPU above CPU in both the SSR card (local-murakumo.infer-view/node-card) and the live
          JS poller's renderNode — GPU renders first now, CPU second"
  :reason "GPU is the meaningful utilization signal for an inference fleet; CPU is dominated by the
          concurrent xmrig mining load noted in decision :2-collector above, so leading with CPU was
          visually prioritizing the less relevant number"
  :repo "orgs/gftdcojp/local-murakumo — no schema/route change, pure view-ordering fix"}

 :addendum-2026-07-05-part2-offline-node-investigation
 {:trigger "user asked why dan/joseph/levi/simeon show offline on the dashboard"
  :method "direct SSH from this machine timed out for all four (consistent with the dashboard's
          reachable:false), then cross-checked against `tailscale status` independently of the
          hwmetrics collector/SSH path entirely"
  :finding "all four show `offline, last seen 1d ago` in tailscale status itself — genuinely powered
           off/asleep at the network layer, not an SSH quirk or a dashboard bug. The other 6 mesh nodes
           (asher, benjamin, gad, issachar, judah, naphtali, zebulun) show active/reachable."
  :verdict "dashboard is reporting correctly; this reconfirms decision :1-precision-and-placement's
           and ADR-2607051431's existing note that not all 10 fleet.edn nodes are kept awake at once —
           no fix needed, no bug"}}
